codex
The rising-branch root and the domain bounds are algebraically correct for ordinary finite inputs. The main gap so far is enforcement: the OpenMS loader can bypass the new temperature check and convert TOF indices beyond the checked range. I’m checking concrete counterexamples and whether they affect the supplied real runs.
