codex
The Python golden test passes all 270 cases. I also found an all-finite synthetic row that passes the domain check but produces a negative discriminant: rounding loses the safety margin when the check adds it to a very large `C0`. None of the supplied PXD029836 rows is close to that failure. The four spectrum digest pins remain unverified, so the changelog’s claim that they reproduce is premature.
